{% comment %}
  Font declarations, shared by every layout.

  Usage:
    {% render 'suf-fonts', apply: true %}        <- declares faces, applies Arial
    {% render 'suf-fonts', apply: true, family: "'Hanken Grotesk', Arial, sans-serif" %}

  The faces are always declared; a browser only downloads a font something
  actually uses, so declaring on a layout that does not apply them costs
  nothing. `family` chooses what the applying rules set, which is how Hanken
  Grotesk is live on layout/suf.liquid while layout/theme.liquid stays on Arial
  until the ~30 legacy templates have been reviewed.

  The applying rules carry !important because both layouts load
  dt-framework.css, which sets font-family on the same elements at higher
  specificity.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  WHY NOT INDIVISIBLE
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  All four Indivisible files -- both .woff and both .woff2, in this repo AND in
  the live theme, byte-identical -- were destroyed by a UTF-8 text round trip.
  Every byte >= 0x80 became U+FFFD (EF BF BD), inflating each file ~75% past
  the length its own header declares. A structural decode finds 0 of 15 WOFF
  tables readable: tags read "=o?=" and "Nloc" rather than "cmap" and "glyf".
  No browser can parse them, and the substitution is lossy, so they cannot be
  repaired. The site rendered in Arial for years as a result.

  Hanken Grotesk replaces it: OFL-licensed, self-hosted, 400 and 700, woff2,
  latin subset, 27 KB for the pair. Self-hosted rather than linked from
  Google's CDN -- two fewer origins on the critical path, and Google Fonts
  sends visitor IPs to Google. See docs/migration.md.

  Both files were verified before being committed: signature wOF2, declared
  length equal to actual byte length, zero U+FFFD sequences. Do that check on
  any font added here.
{% endcomment %}
{%- assign family = family | default: 'Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif' -%}
<style>
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk';
    src: url("{{ 'hanken-grotesk-400.woff2' | asset_url }}") format('woff2');
    font-display: swap;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk';
    src: url("{{ 'hanken-grotesk-700.woff2' | asset_url }}") format('woff2');
    font-display: swap;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  {%- if apply -%}
    p, blockquote, li, a, body, footer, aside, nav, section, article, div, span,
    input, button, textarea, label {
      font-family: {{ family }} !important;
      font-weight: 400;
    }
    h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, strong, b, th {
      font-family: {{ family }} !important;
      font-weight: 700;
    }
  {%- endif -%}
</style>
